1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,790
Sorry, Robbie. Sorry to be late this morning,

2
00:00:02,790 --> 00:00:06,364
but, well, we've still got some time for a cup of coffee.

3
00:00:06,364 --> 00:00:08,814
I can't wait to see my old pal Charley Rafer.

4
00:00:08,814 --> 00:00:23,518
Neither can I.

5
00:00:23,518 --> 00:00:25,300
So you thought about it, huh?

6
00:00:25,300 --> 00:00:27,225
Yes, I have, Dad.

7
00:00:27,225 --> 00:00:28,080
Well, I'm glad.

8
00:00:28,080 --> 00:00:29,532
I knew you'd realize

9
00:00:29,532 --> 00:00:32,497
that this interview could be an important experience for you.

10
00:00:32,497 --> 00:00:35,411
I came to that conclusion.

11
00:00:35,411 --> 00:00:37,924
That's very wise, Robbie.

12
00:00:37,924 --> 00:00:40,570
Very wise.

13
00:00:40,570 --> 00:00:44,215
Now let's head off for the city and the university club.

14
00:00:44,215 --> 00:00:45,770
Thanks, Dad.

15
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:47,963
Thanks ... for what?

16
00:00:47,963 --> 00:00:50,599
Thanks for hearing me out. And ...

17
00:00:50,599 --> 00:00:52,134
And ...?

18
00:00:52,134 --> 00:00:55,130
And thanks for being such an understanding father.

19
00:00:55,130 --> 00:01:12,892
Well, thank you, Robbie. Thank you.

20
00:01:12,892 --> 00:01:14,478
Philip Stewart!

21
00:01:14,478 --> 00:01:15,807
It's great to see you!

22
00:01:15,807 --> 00:01:23,622
Charley Rafer--you look as young as ever.

23
00:01:23,622 --> 00:01:24,899
You must be Robbie.

24
00:01:24,899 --> 00:01:26,763
Hi.

25
00:01:26,763 --> 00:01:29,687
Yes, this is my youngest son Robbie.

26
00:01:29,687 --> 00:01:31,170
Robbie, I want you to meet

27
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:35,093
one of the best tennis players on the Michigan team--

28
00:01:35,093 --> 00:01:36,009
Charley Rafer.

29
00:01:36,009 --> 00:01:37,543
Nice to meet you, Dean Rafer.

30
00:01:37,543 --> 00:01:40,622
Well, are you as good a tennis player as your dad?

31
00:01:40,622 --> 00:01:43,372
No, I'm not very good at it.

32
00:01:43,372 --> 00:01:45,658
Frankly, neither was I.

33
00:01:45,658 --> 00:01:48,345
Charley was the star of the team.

34
00:01:48,345 --> 00:01:49,972
Yeah. Thanks.

35
00:01:49,972 --> 00:01:51,774
Well, how're you been, Philip?

36
00:01:51,774 --> 00:01:54,317
Oh, working too hard.

37
00:01:54,317 --> 00:01:55,635
Doesn't show.

38
00:01:55,635 --> 00:01:56,809
How's Ellen?

39
00:01:56,809 --> 00:01:59,301
Fine, thank you.

40
00:01:59,301 --> 00:02:01,330
And how's Marge?

41
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:04,470
She's still giving the toughest English history exams

42
00:02:04,470 --> 00:02:08,754
in the school and loving every minute of it.

43
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,216
And speaking of minutes,

44
00:02:10,216 --> 00:02:12,131
I have interviews until noon,

45
00:02:12,131 --> 00:02:15,354
so why don't we get right to work?

46
00:02:15,354 --> 00:02:17,681
Can you have lunch with us later?

47
00:02:17,681 --> 00:02:19,607
I'd love to, Philip, but I'm afraid I can't.

48
00:02:19,607 --> 00:02:20,956
I'm only here two days,

49
00:02:20,956 --> 00:02:23,890
and I have interviews with twenty-six applicants.

50
00:02:23,890 --> 00:02:25,136
I understand.

51
00:02:25,136 --> 00:02:26,434
Well, thanks.

52
00:02:26,434 --> 00:02:29,955
I'll wait outside.

53
00:02:29,955 --> 00:02:32,035
Good luck, Son.

54
00:02:32,035 --> 00:02:33,642
Did you bring your transcript from high school?

55
00:02:33,642 --> 00:02:34,352
Yes, sir.

56
00:02:34,352 --> 00:02:35,299
Right here.

57
00:02:35,299 --> 00:02:37,853
Thank you.

58
00:02:37,853 --> 00:02:44,196
Please sit down.

59
00:02:44,196 --> 00:02:45,390
I see under "activities" that

60
00:02:45,390 --> 00:02:47,234
you've been writing for the school paper.

61
00:02:47,234 --> 00:02:49,180
Yes, sir.

62
00:02:49,180 --> 00:02:50,940
What kinds of articles have you written?

63
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:55,832
All kinds--sports, editorials, theater reviews.

64
00:02:55,832 --> 00:02:57,572
You name it, I've written it.

65
00:02:57,572 --> 00:02:59,302
Hmmm.

66
00:02:59,302 --> 00:03:01,804
Well, have you ever thought of becoming a journalist?

67
00:03:01,804 --> 00:03:03,874
A professional writer?

68
00:03:03,874 --> 00:03:06,427
Not until recently.

69
00:03:06,427 --> 00:03:09,228
Michigan has a fine School of Journalism.

70
00:03:09,228 --> 00:03:12,667
Yes, I know that.

71
00:03:12,667 --> 00:03:15,190
You seem to have some reservations.

72
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:19,432
I'm a little uncertain.

73
00:03:19,432 --> 00:03:21,224
It's been very nice talking to you.

74
00:03:21,224 --> 00:03:24,087
Nice talking to you, sir.

75
00:03:24,087 --> 00:03:26,856
One piece of advice.

76
00:03:26,856 --> 00:03:31,439
The most important thing is for you to decide your own future.

77
00:03:31,439 --> 00:03:33,313
Yes, sir.

78
00:03:33,313 --> 00:03:34,435
Good-bye, Dean Rafer.

79
00:03:34,435 --> 00:03:34,435
Good-bye, Robbie. Good luck.
